WEBVTT

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.620
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Thursday the twelfth. Can you all hear me?</v>

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:13.730
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah. Thought I was on mute then. Usually am when I've got something useful to say.</v>

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:21.149
<v Sarah Okafor>While we're waiting for everyone to settle, the heating in the portakabin — honestly, my tea's warmer than the radiator.</v>

00:00:21.489 --> 00:00:29.190
<v Jamie Brennan>The heating in the portakabin's purely decorative, that is. I've still got my coat on. Just moaning, not putting a job in.</v>

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:33.869
<v Marcus Hale>Very smart coat, though. Really lifts the whole stores operation.</v>

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:42.750
<v Grace Liu>Sorry, I'm here. Traffic on the ring road was dreadful. Sat looking at the same brake lights for absolutely ages.</v>

00:00:44.859 --> 00:00:48.359
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, you haven't missed anything technical. Just the coat review.</v>

00:00:50.039 --> 00:00:54.240
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, enough of that. Finished bits first, then what we're actually agreeing.</v>

00:00:55.359 --> 00:00:59.909
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah so, finished the repair on the fire panel last night. That's done.</v>

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:04.060
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Fi. Closed, then, not another one for today's list.</v>

00:01:05.969 --> 00:01:11.920
<v Fiona Doyle>And I tested the GT1 compressor yesterday and it's all fine now. That testing's finished as well.</v>

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:15.650
<v Marcus Hale>Right, good. That's the compressor test put to bed.</v>

00:01:16.599 --> 00:01:26.400
<v Fiona Doyle>Only other thing from me on the running side: saw the pressure on the line 3 barrel dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:33.150
<v Aisha Begum>Mm, a transient dip, then. You're reporting what happened, not asking for another adjustment?</v>

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:39.840
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, just an observation here. No new action coming out of that.</v>

00:01:40.989 --> 00:01:48.689
<v Grace Liu>And I signed off the inspection on the dryer on Tuesday. That's already complete, in case it's still showing in anyone's notes.</v>

00:01:49.819 --> 00:01:51.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine, dryer inspection done. Thanks.</v>

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:59.780
<v Hannah Price>Um, my blocker hasn't changed. Can't get to the number two bearing until production gives us a window.</v>

00:02:01.849 --> 00:02:06.750
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, there isn't a production window confirmed. Can't pretend there's access when there isn't.</v>

00:02:08.419 --> 00:02:12.620
<v Hannah Price>Exactly. So that's blocked, not me committing to get on it today.</v>

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:19.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Keep that separate from the other bearing item, please, or we'll tie ourselves in knots.</v>

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:26.659
<v Fiona Doyle>On that other one, I'll grease and check the bearings on the GT2 bearing tomorrow. It's fairly important.</v>

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:32.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Fi. That's the GT2 bearing with you, then, fairly important and tomorrow.</v>

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:35.879
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, tomorrow. I'll do that one.</v>

00:02:37.069 --> 00:02:42.319
<v Marcus Hale>Right, two different bearing conversations. Teams captions will still make a complete meal of it.</v>

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:49.400
<v Sarah Okafor>Han, can you send the shift handover report round tomorrow morning? Not an emergency but don't let it slip.</v>

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.340
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll send the shift handover report round tomorrow morning.</v>

00:02:53.879 --> 00:02:59.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Doesn't need everyone dropping what they're doing, just don't lose it in the shuffle.</v>

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.780
<v Hannah Price>No, understood. That's with me.</v>

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:10.770
<v Sarah Okafor>And Han, can you book a contractor to look at the Gas Turbine 1? That's fairly important.</v>

00:03:11.939 --> 00:03:17.539
<v Hannah Price>Yes, I'll book a contractor to look at the Gas Turbine 1. Fairly important, got it.</v>

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:24.800
<v Jamie Brennan>Sorry, talking over you — that's the booking you're taking, not automatically going out with them?</v>

00:03:26.939 --> 00:03:31.840
<v Hannah Price>The booking, yeah. I'm accepting that bit, not volunteering for a visit as well.</v>

00:03:32.919 --> 00:03:38.870
<v Marcus Hale>And the Gas Turbine 1 contractor item doesn't mean we're reopening that finished compressor test, does it?</v>

00:03:40.419 --> 00:03:44.270
<v Fiona Doyle>No. The GT1 compressor test I mentioned is done. Separate item.</v>

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:55.750
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. We also need someone to do a site visit at Northfield with the contractor after lunch. Not an emergency but don't let it slip. Anyone able to take that?</v>

00:03:57.969 --> 00:04:02.169
<v Aisha Begum>I can't take the visit, sorry. Don't count me in for that.</v>

00:04:03.550 --> 00:04:07.400
<v Marcus Hale>Nor me. I can't offer to be off site after lunch.</v>

00:04:08.949 --> 00:04:11.400
<v Jamie Brennan>I'm not able to take it either.</v>

00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:20.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, the Northfield visit after lunch is still needed, but nobody's taken it. Unowned, not agreed against someone's name.</v>

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:27.560
<v Hannah Price>And just to be absolutely clear, my contractor booking isn't an acceptance of that visit.</v>

00:04:29.529 --> 00:04:31.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, understood. Keeping the two separate.</v>

00:04:32.509 --> 00:04:40.209
<v Grace Liu>I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the 11kV board today at 2pm. Drop everything for that one — that's the priority.</v>

00:04:41.529 --> 00:04:48.879
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Grace Liu. The lock-out tag-out sign-off on the 11kV board is yours, today at 2pm. Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:04:50.899 --> 00:04:56.500
<v Marcus Hale>Two o'clock today, yep. Heard you clearly that time; your audio went a bit watery earlier.</v>

00:04:57.939 --> 00:05:03.540
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, today at 2pm. And what I'm taking is the sign-off, just so the wording's right.</v>

00:05:04.379 --> 00:05:09.980
<v Aisha Begum>Right, that's the one at the top, rather than everything on the list being called urgent.</v>

00:05:10.449 --> 00:05:12.899
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Otherwise urgent just means absolutely nothing.</v>

00:05:13.209 --> 00:05:23.709
<v Jamie Brennan>There's also the purchase order for the AC1 needing a chase by the 28th. Whenever you get a chance sort of priority. I'm flagging the gap, not taking it on.</v>

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:27.910
<v Sarah Okafor>Anyone able to own chasing the purchase order for the AC1?</v>

00:05:30.189 --> 00:05:35.790
<v Jamie Brennan>Not me, I'm afraid. I know it's a stores-shaped thing, but I can't commit to it.</v>

00:05:37.399 --> 00:05:39.850
<v Fiona Doyle>I can't take that as well, sorry.</v>

00:05:42.089 --> 00:05:49.790
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, nobody on the AC1 purchase order chase, then. Still by the 28th, whenever you get a chance, but no owner agreed.</v>

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:56.959
<v Aisha Begum>Good to say that out loud. Silence on Teams can look an awful lot like agreement.</v>

00:05:57.769 --> 00:06:01.620
<v Jamie Brennan>Exactly. Me mentioning it wasn't a quiet promise to do it.</v>

00:06:02.399 --> 00:06:13.949
<v Sarah Okafor>Quick check before we finish. Han: shift handover report round tomorrow morning, not an emergency but don't let it slip; and book a contractor to look at the Gas Turbine 1, fairly important.</v>

00:06:14.709 --> 00:06:20.310
<v Hannah Price>Yes, both accepted. Report tomorrow morning, and the contractor booking. No visit attached to my name.</v>

00:06:22.629 --> 00:06:28.579
<v Fiona Doyle>And I'll grease and check the bearings on the GT2 bearing tomorrow. Fairly important. That's my one.</v>

00:06:30.149 --> 00:06:36.100
<v Grace Liu>Mine's the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the 11kV board, today at 2pm. Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:06:37.189 --> 00:06:52.939
<v Sarah Okafor>And still unowned: do a site visit at Northfield with the contractor after lunch — not an emergency but don't let it slip — and chase the purchase order for the AC1 by the 28th, whenever you get a chance. Neither has been picked up.</v>

00:06:54.839 --> 00:06:58.339
<v Marcus Hale>Yep. Clear enough. And the completed stuff stays completed, thankfully.</v>

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:01.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, that's us. Thanks, everyone.</v>
